@prefix as:       <https://www.w3.org/ns/activitystreams#> .
@prefix mem:      <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/ontology/mem#> .
@prefix prov:     <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix xsd:      <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdfs:     <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:      <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix skos:     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix prof:     <http://www.w3.org/ns/dx/prof/> .
@prefix wiki:     <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/ontology/wiki#> .
@prefix wikirole: <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/ontology/wikirole#> .

# ===========================================================================
# Proposal 02 — GATED CONCEPTUAL-STRUCTURE EXTENSION (construction, not staleness).
# Prerequisite for proposal 03. Adds the type + role that the 9 untyped
# SPARQL-SELECT lookup affordances need but which DO NOT EXIST yet.
#
# This is a judgment call flagged explicitly for human review (playbook
# §"No existing type or role fits"). Forcing the lookups under wiki:SearchAffordance
# would be wrong and would fail SHACL; a clean gated extension grows the graph.
# ===========================================================================

<urn:uuid:7c1a0d20-5e44-4f3b-9a01-2026052302>
    a as:Announce, mem:RealignAction, prov:Activity ;
    as:actor <urn:agent:claude-code> ;
    as:target </vault/wiki/working/curator-proposals/> ;
    as:object </vault/ontology/wiki> ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith <urn:agent:claude-code> ;
    prov:used </vault/ontology/wiki> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom </vault/meta/affordances/contact-find-by-name.ttl> ;
    mem:stalenessClass mem:ProseDrift ;
    mem:rationale """Nine catalog descriptors (8 contact/org lookups + bridge-card-to-wiki) are flagged
descriptor:untyped. Each is a CLIENT-RUN, PARAMETERIZED SPARQL-SELECT lookup: typed only wiki:Affordance,
carrying sh:agentInstruction + wiki:selectQuery + a $param. To bring them under the descriptor contract
(AffordanceDescriptorShape) they need a concrete wiki:*Affordance subtype AND a prof:hasRole from the
wikirole scheme. I checked the existing options and NONE fit:
  - wiki:SearchAffordance is for HTTP-DISPATCH query surfaces — its SHACL (SearchAffordanceShape)
    REQUIRES wiki:dispatchPattern (^\\?ext=...) + wiki:targetContainer. The lookups have neither; they
    are run in the agent's own Comunica engine (the Pod hosts no SPARQL endpoint). Typing them
    SearchAffordance would FAIL validation. (playbook explicitly warns against this misfit.)
  - wiki:DerivedNavigationAffordance carries wiki:selectQuery but its semantics are 'compute a derived
    NAVIGATION view (breadcrumbs, MOC indexes)'. A by-key contact/org lookup derives no navigation
    structure; it is a retrieval, not a view. Misfit.
  - wiki:DerivedClassAffordance derives an rdf:type (wiki:constructQuery). Lookups derive no class. Misfit.
  - wikirole scheme has affordance / write- / version- / derived-class- / derived-navigation- roles
    plus synthesis roles (overview, operation-log, ...). There is NO query/lookup role.
This is a genuine conceptual-structure GAP, not a misfiling. Per the class-extension contract (D100,
wiki:ClassExtensionShape) the conceptual structure is extensible data; the correct repair is a GATED
extension: a new rooted subclass + a new in-scheme role concept, landed in working/ for SHACL validation
(inference='none') + higher-trust review before crystallizing. prov:used = the wiki vocab itself
(authoritative for the type lattice).""" ;
    as:published "2026-05-23T22:34:12Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

# --- Proposed new class (satisfies wiki:ClassExtensionShape: subClassOf + label + comment) ----
# REPO-SIDE: add to overlays/wiki-memory/vocabulary/wiki.ttl (so `make reset` reproduces it).
wiki:QueryAffordance
    a rdfs:Class, owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf wiki:Affordance ;          # rooting: wiki:Affordance reaches wiki:Resource
    rdfs:label "Query affordance" ;
    rdfs:comment "Affordance descriptor for a parameterized, CLIENT-RUN SPARQL-SELECT lookup over Pod content (e.g. find a contact card by name/email/ORCID, find the wiki page bridging a card). Carries a wiki:selectQuery with a named parameter ($name, $email, $card, ...) the agent substitutes, and an sh:agentInstruction naming the source graph(s) and how to pass the parameter. Distinct from wiki:SearchAffordance (HTTP ?ext= dispatch surface, requires wiki:dispatchPattern) and from wiki:DerivedNavigationAffordance (computes a navigation view, not a by-key retrieval): a QueryAffordance neither dispatches over HTTP nor derives structure — it retrieves existing resources by key, executed in the agent's own SPARQL engine since the Pod hosts no endpoint." ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/ontology/wiki> ;
    skos:scopeNote "Used as rdf:type (alongside prof:ResourceDescriptor) on the contact/org lookup and card-bridge descriptors served from the addressbook overlay. Payload predicate: wiki:selectQuery. Pairs with prof:hasRole wikirole:query-affordance." .

# --- Proposed new role concept (in the wikirole SKOS scheme; broader :affordance) -------------
# REPO-SIDE: add to overlays/<the file that ships wikirole> (same file as :write-affordance etc.).
wikirole:query-affordance
    a owl:NamedIndividual , skos:Concept , prof:ResourceRole ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/ontology/wikirole> ;
    skos:inScheme <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/ontology/wikirole> ;
    skos:broader wikirole:affordance ;
    skos:prefLabel "Query affordance" ;
    skos:definition "An affordance that performs a parameterized client-run SPARQL-SELECT lookup over Pod content, retrieving existing resources by key. The agent substitutes the named parameter and runs the query in its own engine; the Pod hosts no SPARQL endpoint. Distinct from the HTTP-dispatch search role and from derived-view roles." .

# --- Notes for the reviewer ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. ClassExtensionShape step (3) 'register class -> container in Type Index' is N/A here: affordance
#    descriptor classes are META-LEVEL (served from /meta/affordances/), not content classes with an
#    instance container. The existing wiki:*Affordance subtypes are likewise unregistered in the Type
#    Index. Steps (1) rooted subClassOf, (2) shaped by AffordanceDescriptorShape, (4) label+comment
#    all hold. Confirm this meta-vs-content distinction is acceptable.
# 2. Validate this proposal's wiki:QueryAffordance node against wiki:ClassExtensionShape with
#    inference="none" (RDFS entailment would trivially satisfy the rooting check — see the shape's
#    own sh:agentInstruction).
# 3. Once crystallized, proposal 03 retypes the 9 descriptors against this new type + role.
